@[refind page]
rEFInd is a boot menu for UEFI machines (not BIOS). It finds the kernels in
/boot by itself and starts them directly (the kernel has EFI boot support). It
isn't on this ISO: cast it with network (see @[todo boot-loader]).

The EFI system partition must be mounted at /boot/efi in the target. Then in
@[enchantment chroot]:
 @[refind-install]
That copies rEFInd to the EFI partition, adds a driver for /boot's
filesystem, and creates a firmware boot entry. rEFInd needs the kernel
options in /boot/refind_linux.conf (one line per menu entry: a title, then
the options):
 @[blkid -s PARTUUID -o value /dev/sda2]   # your root partition's PARTUUID
 @[echo '"Source Mage" "root=PARTUUID=PUT-IT-HERE rw"' > /boot/refind_linux.conf]
(@[mkrlconf] would copy the options this ISO booted with: wrong here.)
 @[exit]

Not yet tested on this ISO: please report what works and what doesn't.

